    "summary": "Smoking 'They Love Each Other', epic 'Eyes Of The World', monster He’s Gone→Truckin′→The Other One jam",
    "blurb": "The marathon at Kezar delivers smoking \"They Love Each Other\" and an expansive \"Eyes Of The World\". Highlights include the seamless He’s Gone → Truckin' → The Other One → Eyes sequence and a bright set two with Here Comes Sunshine. Soundboard recordings capture the high‑energy flow throughout all three sets.",
    "review": "May 26, 1973 at Kezar Stadium finds the Dead in top form during one of their most ambitious three‑set marathons. Jerry’s guitar is on fire from the opening “The Promised Land” through the soaring “They Love Each Other,” while Phil lays down ultrawizardry bass that propels the long jams, especially his solo in The Other One. Keith Godchaux supplies a solid piano/organ backdrop with occasional Rhodes sparkle, and Bill Kreutzmann’s drumming drives the show from the first beat, keeping the momentum relentless. Set two shines with “Here Comes Sunshine” and a flawless China Cat Sunflower → I Know You Rider transition, while set three erupts into a legendary He’s Gone → Truckin' → The Other One → Eyes Of The World → China Doll sequence that still feels fresh. The show ends on a high note with “Sugar Magnolia” and a classic encore of “Casey Jones,” making this Kezar run a must‑listen for any 1973 enthusiast.",
